  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+1 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{1}{3})=-0.339\\,836\u2026\u2248-0.3398\n$$\n\nSince $-0.3398$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.3398.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.3398.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.3398.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/ed9b300e3f4f79298feba6a2d61347d938ce64d7100ad7b0696e13dbe2a65238.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.3398 \\\\  & \u22483.4814\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & \u22483.4814-2\\pi \u2248-2.8018\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248-2.8,\\,x\u2248-0.3.\n$$",
